{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena","id":1371898,"title":"Exalted vs. Optimisation (Split from Exalted: Arena)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-29T05:11:15-08:00","id":1371898,"title":"Exalted vs. Optimisation (Split from Exalted: Arena)","content":"Okay so this was a pretty significant tangent from the topic at hand so I split it off so as not to impede the intended role of the Exalted: Arena thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:21:01-08:00","id":1371899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370624#post1370624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the game is designed with the idea that some players might have a defense of 2-3. In my experience this is not the case, usually people have 6, some have 7, others have 5, almost never do they have as little as 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like the game was designed for a completely different chargen mechanism, then they went and changed things so everyone would have half a dozen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T05:13:27-08:00","id":1371955,"title":"","content":"And it's a mess! Well done forum software, well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T05:37:14-08:00","id":1371959,"title":"","content":"Well, was still worth a shot, thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T05:55:40-08:00","id":1371963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's a case of using the wrong opponents. There's no need to add four dice to a Blood Ape when you can fight Octavian. There's no need to add four dice to Octavian when you can fight Ligier. There's no need to add four dice to Ligier when you can fight the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point.<br /> A Blood Ape is a terrifying opponent for a mortal. Giant demon apes aren't there to terrify Exalted though. My Essence 2 Lunars fought a Battle Group of Blood Apes on a zeppelin; it was a cool fight, lots of cool stunts, lasted about 3 rounds. In the last round, several of the PCs literally did nothing so that the Ape-Totem PC could face off against the biggest demon Ape.<br /> <br /> And that's fine. The battle wasn't there to make PCs badly injured. It was to a)show that the bad guys are putting in some effort to stopping people reaching the McGuffin before them, b)show that the bad guys use demons, and c)have a cool fight on a Zeppelin.<br /> <br /> The following session, one single non-combat optimised PC fought a storm serpent, while the other PCs watched. Not just any storm serpent, but the biggest storm serpent around.<br /> This combat lasted longer, like 7 rounds or so, and it wasn't extremely easy, but I don't think anyone was shocked when Krove the Tiger-Bull, Strongest In All The Land, proved himself stronger than a storm serpent and it ran off to cry to its friends.<br /> Again, that's fine. The point wasn't to give Krove an extremely difficult fight, it was to a)show that the Elemental Pole of Air has lots of scary storm elementals nearby, b)have PCs work together to solve a problem using brains and brawn (the No Moon established a fact that if they did a special ritual, then defeated the biggest storm serpent around, the other storm serpents would leave them alone), and c)have a cool fight on a Zeppelin.<br /> <br /> The fight after that was a few PCs attacking 100 assorted minor demons to save two Dragonblood. It lasted 2 rounds. The point was to a)show that there's a ton of demons invading the palace they were in, b)let the Full Moon viking and Changing Moon archer show off their combat skills, and c)have the PCs save some Dragonblood who are too injured to fight them, so they can talk to the Dragonblood and find out some stuff.<br /> <br /> The fight after that... lasted 7 or 8 rounds, and by the end all but 2 of the PCs were incapacitated. That was a fight in a giant cold hazard against some Yama Kings; 6 ancient sun-demons who'd escaped from Hell having been trapped there for 1500 years by the Dragons, and were trying to kill the Elemental Dragon of Air (possibly in revenge, possibly because of the eternal winter that's gripping the world). <i>That</i> was the fight that was supposed to be difficult and challenging, because it was the finale fight of that story arc.<br /> <br /> Similarly, in my old game, the PCs sometimes fought battle groups of humans, first-circle demons, elementals, etc... that's not supposed to be challenging. Second-circle demons and the mile-high, three-headed behemoth they accidentally released... that's challenging.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this... I do, therefore, agree with a point DrLoveMonkey made earlier. If the above is the case, why do the writers keep releasing fully fleshed-out mechanically-written serious antagonists for mortals? Or 13 year-old Dragonblood?<br /> I've got a folder full of wacky creatures with interesting ideas for powers, that are entirely inappropriate antagonists for a circle of Solars, except maybe in groups of 100 (where their interesting powers get turned into Might anyway).<br /> I don't need a lot of stats for interesting flavour and scene-setting creatures. Just fluff description is fine, because I can pull &quot;Yeah, they roll 7 dice and their defence is 4&quot; out of my head.<br /> The only Hundred Devils Night Parade entries I've used are animals (for Lunars), and a little bit the demons and elementals (if PCs summon them). I planned to use Mahicara, and there are a couple of other behemoths that'd be suitable. Other than that, I've got a lot of nice PDFs that I just don't really need for this game. Similarly, the book has all these rules for animals that... honestly, you could run with 5 dice pools (like 2nd ed did them). A lot of their cool abilities just don't come up that much, unless you're a Lunar.<br /> What actually is useful as antagonists for a circle of PCs is stuff like behemoths and second-circle demons; not that they should be doing this every session, but that's what I need a complicated pdf with a bunch of stats and mechanically-interesting abilities for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T06:13:46-08:00","id":1371965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371222#post1371222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[EDIT]<br /> <br /> Does your character concept need those Charms? Because Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defence on Melee 3/Dex 3 makes you pretty deadly. Yes, you can't shoot beams of golden light from your sword... but you don't need to if your Twilight Scholar is fighting Brides of Ahlat, Fog Sharks and Claw Striders. Intermediate combat skill is enough.<br /> <br /> Give that Twilight plenty of chance to use Lore and Medicine Charms -- start them on the Wyld Shaping Charm tree and Sorcerous Workings and they probably won't buy combat abilities if they already feel badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you have to be in the Wyld, or near it, to use Wyld shaping charms? <br /> <br /> I think the difficulty in using some of the other systems to properly feel badass is a big part of the puzzle. In my first-time game, it took me a long time to figure out how to use introducing facts properly, and I still haven't really figured out sorcerous workings. Your character can be a badass at social influence or something but it takes significantly more skill to feel like that in play than for combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because that's Dragon Ball Z. PCs and ST in an arms race. The players want to succeed, the ST doesn't let them, PCs get bigger numbers, ST gets bigger numbers until every random encounter is between war gods who can destroy planets with a gesture. </div> </div> </div>For me a big reason to boost combat was not a failure in combat, exactly, but combats with long periods where I was pretty our characters were going to die. The reason for this was not the ST's desire not to let us succeed but instead the ST's desire to make fun / exciting encounters, and maybe overshooting on power level a little. Maybe this was also due to us being high enough on power level at the start that the combat system is a little wonky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the PCs want to be good at something, arbitrarily upping the difficulty to under-cut them is bad form. </div> </div> </div>I think (as some have mentioned before in this thread) a lot of people don't particularly care, in the abstract, how good their characters are at combat, they just want to have fun during combat encounters. In a lot of games this can be accomplished by taking the cool-looking combat powers you see and not thinking particularly hard about optimization. In Exalted this might be a trap. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's a case of using the wrong opponents. There's no need to add four dice to a Blood Ape when you can fight Octavian. There's no need to add four dice to Octavian when you can fight Ligier. There's no need to add four dice to Ligier when you can fight the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you really like an iconic enemy but your PCs are overspecced to deal with them, you can just up their stats. But if you're doing that every encounter you're really going to wonk the power-curve. </div> </div> </div>You can also use multiple opponents to help with this to an extent. Even Saitama will have trouble fighting 5 DB's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T07:39:46-08:00","id":1371972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I can't answer exactly Apromor exactly when you ask him &quot;Why the Solar tools do not make fight interesting ?&quot; and I think the answer is simple (and greatly explained by habitableexoplanet) : people want challenging fights that are fun and exciting. <br /> <br /> To take a simple example : Take DD4. When you start DD4, the fights have very few options, so you feel your character is not necessarily &quot;weak&quot; but simple. The fights usually last 4-5 rounds against enemies who don't have very special abilities or comeback powers. <br /> Then, 25 levels later, when you are on your way to godhood, you have multiple options for your character (I don't remember exactly but something along the lines of 2 at-will, 4 encounters, 4 dailies, multiple objects powers, special features of your class and parangonic path and epic path), you feel your character is usually strong and has some layers of complexity. And the fights are usually not down to Round 1 everyone unleashes everything and the fight is over, but will regularly lasts 4-5 rounds as well, or will have multiple phases against enemies like Lolth, where you have enough time and space to express the power of your character, and usually have multiple tactical choices to make. <br /> <br /> I think the experience most people have with Solar tools is you one shot-people very dead, for a very long range of different opponent, and thus fights are not the interesting &quot;back and forth&quot; you expect them to be because that's what you think when you read the book but is more along the lines of : Roll 15 initiative, Attack first with TAP against any very impressive antagonist and some Charms, deal 20 damage, done. It goes very far from the expected experience of &quot;the more power you have the more original and fun encounters you will make against your enemies&quot;.<br /> <br /> I understand that some of these tools exist in the game (Octavian can't be oneshoted, Ahlat is certainly very strong but I've never read him in great details, etc ...) but they are not easy to master for the ST (it took me 2 years and a half to finally make a fight I was proud of against a Circle of 4 Solars with custom enemies because it was very tense and dramatic), and furthermore they do not exist in any reusable fashion like any DD monster generator for a specific challenge level you can't to play out. I can only understand people that didn't push the experience as far as me to try and tweak the enemies and read enough content to get their satisfaction the way they wanted it and I really can't blame them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:11:45-08:00","id":1371979,"title":"","content":"I feel it's very important to note that a key difference between level 1 and level 25 DnD is that at level 1 you're fighting goblins, and at level 25 archdemons. This is extremely important.<br /> <br /> Playing a combat Solar is like starting at level... 15, I guess. But the antagonists written up for Exalted don't include nearly enough lvl 15-25 stuff.<br /> <br /> And as you say, it's possible, but hard, to make that yourself.<br /> <br /> I guess though the other thing with DnD is that five level 10 Fighters are probably all going to be roughly similar in combat power. Whereas five Essence 1 Solars can vary massively in combat power. And there's good reasons for that, but it can be awkward for the ST and players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:22:05-08:00","id":1371981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1371972#post1371972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the experience most people have with Solar tools is you one shot-people very dead, for a very long range of different opponent, and thus fights are not the interesting &quot;back and forth&quot; you expect them to be because that's what you think when you read the book but is more along the lines of : Roll 15 initiative, Attack first with TAP against any very impressive antagonist and some Charms, deal 20 damage, done. It goes very far from the expected experience of &quot;the more power you have the more original and fun encounters you will make against your enemies&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried, you know, <i>not</i> doing that?<br /> <br /> One of my most memorable Pathfinder experiences was the DM laying out fifteen Hobgoblins when our level 5 characters were down their last three or four hit points. My Cleric used a Domain slot and power to blast out an Empowered Fireball. The look on people's faces when they realised that one-shotted every foe, even if they made their save was priceless.<br /> <br /> But, you know, I didn't do that every fight.<br /> <br /> If Awakening Eye + Thunderbolt Attack Prana is boring to you... don't do it every fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st Edition Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus goes the existance of the Solar Exalted - to wield the power of the Sun, but to do so with the greatest economy possible, showing their true might only when the need is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-29-2020, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:54:55-08:00","id":1371989,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> Yes obviously you are fighting different enemies. But as you said, the number of enemies on the high spectrum of the fighting power is quite low, and this is usually the spectrum where people who play Solar will end up. I guess I need to buy Hundred Devil Night Parade (don't remember the name) to have more antagonists, but I was really disappointed by the NPC section of the core (I don't like the organizing of the pages, the complexity of each NPC, etc ...) so I don't know yet exactly.<br /> It is true Exalts power can vary a lot, but a tendency is usually to have very good level of fighting, because people don't like to wait for 2 hours of gameplay looking at someone throwing hundreds of dices. And it's normal.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I have done this once to test the combo, and so I decided I was gonna put TAP a bit further down in the Athletics tree for my next games. I'm fine with the idea of &quot;Don't do this thing if it bothers you&quot; but then you are not really answering to people saying &quot;I'm not happy with the system because it didn't live up to many of our expectations about gameplay&quot;. I think yours is the more sensible answer but I also understand people trying to find different ways to make the system closer to their expectations instead of basically ignoring what bothers you, because it's a sort of an optimization/balance problem and people love to try and solve them when it's about their favorite hobby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:41:44-08:00","id":1372005,"title":"","content":"The good thing about HDNP is that you can buy the entries separately, so just get the behemoths and second-circle demon.<br /> <br /> The Core antagonists actually include some good stuff; Octavian, Ahlat, the Nephwrack. But there's a lot of lesser things that are written as if they're individually useful, whereas they should be written with a view to being battle groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:22:16-08:00","id":1372200,"title":"","content":"I think more people would be willing to build characters poorly suited to combat if it didn\u2019t take up a huge amount of the system, session time and have the consequence of your character dying horribly if you don\u2019t optimize. <br /> <br /> Every combat charm I purchased as a lunar was a concession to not wanting to die in a silly, unsatisfying way because it\u2019s impossible to tell what is a reasonable thing for my character to fight until it\u2019s to late. <br /> <br /> Also, suggesting people simply not use charm combos that are intended to be really good just outlines the fact that the combat rules are failing to work properly, not that the players are at fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:38:29-08:00","id":1372201,"title":"","content":"Since second edition my mantra as a Storyteller has been &quot;split your scenes&quot; don't exhaust yourself building these huge action set pieces for 5 Solars because they\u2019ll be a nightmare to run and probably won\u2019t achieve the payoff you\u2019re looking for.<br /> <br /> My response to an alpha strike is to ask how many motes that cost.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T18:06:31-08:00","id":1372206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372200#post1372200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more people would be willing to build characters poorly suited to combat if it didn\u2019t take up a huge amount of the system, session time and have the consequence of your character dying horribly if you don\u2019t optimize.<br /> <br /> Every combat charm I purchased as a lunar was a concession to not wanting to die in a silly, unsatisfying way because it\u2019s impossible to tell what is a reasonable thing for my character to fight until it\u2019s to late.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with this in Ex3.<br /> <br /> #1 The choice of withering or decisive is a strictly out of character decision. If your Storyteller doesn't think it's kosher to pummel your Twilight with no combat ability to gain initiative to go after the Dawn Caste that's <i>their</i> issue not anything the system says.<br /> #2 If they decide it's dramatically appropriate to go ahead with a decisive attack there's the following to consider-<br /> you can cheat death once per story at the cost of accepting a crippling injury.<br /> #3 Unless they're basically throwing you out the game, killing your character is a burden for the Storyteller too.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see you're playing a two person game which has the potential to make some of these things more of an issue than they would normally be. Yeah, if nobody can fight you've got a problem but for perspective 75% of my currently active PCs are the dead weight of the group combat-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, suggesting people simply not use charm combos that are intended to be really good just outlines the fact that the combat rules are failing to work properly, not that the players are at fault.</div> </div> </div> </div> On this we agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-01-2020, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T18:16:20-08:00","id":1372209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372200#post1372200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more people would be willing to build characters poorly suited to combat if it didn\u2019t take up a huge amount of the system, session time and have the consequence of your character dying horribly if you don\u2019t optimize.</div> </div> </div> </div>This cannot be stated enough. Combat is this sort of black hole of gameplay where somehow every session end up being at least 50% combat and every combat is critical. <br /> I tried, exactly once, making a character who wasn't good at combat for a &quot;high intrigue low combat&quot; game at the GM's recommendation. It did indeed have less combat, but I walked out halfway through the second session's second fight. It was a horrible slog to sit around doing nothing meaningful except almost dying because I didn't build a murderhobo. <br /> <br /> EVERY other subsystem can be worked around, roleplayed around, the works. You can build a ship, steal a ship, buy a ship, get a pirate to let you ride his ship, conjure a cloud-chariot, etc, or even just give up and decide you don't want to cross that ocean. But nope, gotta fight those fights no alternatives allowed except character death. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372200#post1372200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every combat charm I purchased as a lunar was a concession to not wanting to die in a silly, unsatisfying way because it\u2019s impossible to tell what is a reasonable thing for my character to fight until it\u2019s to late.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too find it absurd that TTRPGs seem utterly terrified of a seasoned warrior having the slightest clue about the capabilities of his opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T23:27:41-08:00","id":1372228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372209#post1372209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This cannot be stated enough. Combat is this sort of black hole of gameplay where somehow every session end up being at least 50% combat and every combat is critical.<br /> I tried, exactly once, making a character who wasn't good at combat for a &quot;high intrigue low combat&quot; game at the GM's recommendation. It did indeed have less combat, but I walked out halfway through the second session's second fight. It was a horrible slog to sit around doing nothing meaningful except almost dying because I didn't build a murderhobo.<br /> <br /> EVERY other subsystem can be worked around, roleplayed around, the works. You can build a ship, steal a ship, buy a ship, get a pirate to let you ride his ship, conjure a cloud-chariot, etc, or even just give up and decide you don't want to cross that ocean. But nope, gotta fight those fights no alternatives allowed except character death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not found this to be the case at my tables. I usually ST myself but even if I don't we don't have nearly as much combat. I think we had combat about once every 2 or 3 sessions last time I played a bigger group, and multiple of those were quick, not even lasting three rounds?<br /> In addition, we had lots of variations in combat prowess in the group and I don't think anyone was displeased by their power.<br /> <br /> This doesn't sound like a system problem to me. This sounds like a playstyle/ST style issue. Having combat every single session seems really frequent to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T00:24:02-08:00","id":1372230,"title":"","content":"I tend to do an easy combat every 2-3 sessions, and a challenging one every story.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, my Zenith has Defence 4, Soak 3, two Resistance charms and most of Tiger style. It's a low combat, essence 4 game.<br /> <br /> He's lost an eye, arm, and several toes. I'm not sure if that shows that having suboptimal stats for combat is going to put you in big trouble, or that this doesn't matter because you'll still survive.<br /> <br /> Either way, I am going to make my next character better at combat. Or at Disengaging.<br /> <br /> Though, considering that I do have most of Tiger Style, I think maybe the lesson is that first you should buy good base stats (and armour), then you should buy lots of charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-02-2020, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T00:50:19-08:00","id":1372232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372200#post1372200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, suggesting people simply not use charm combos that are intended to be really good just outlines the fact that the combat rules are failing to work properly, not that the players are at fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>TAP is about rushing forward in a blur and turning your momentum into a powerful killing blow. It works exactly as intended and is really good.<br /> <br /> That's not a combat rules problem.<br /> <br /> The problem is that some people don't want to awesomely win fights in one move -- they want a dramatic back and forth struggle.<br /> <br /> Exalted lets you have a dramatic back and forth struggle: look at all the Brawl Charms I listed earlier, look at the ENTIRE Dodge and Resistance tree.<br /> <br /> Exalted does not let you have a dramatic back and forth struggle if you build a character with super-speed designed to kill their enemies in one blow. (Unless, you know, you fight something level appropriate like Octavian.)<br /> <br /> It's like taking Dexterity 5 and complaining your character isn't a bumbling oaf: you can make your character a bumbling oaf if you want, that's not a system problem. You so it by not taking Dexterity 5 -- or even by taking it, but not using it.<br /> <br /> TAP costs Willpower. It's three Charms into the Athletics tree. You have to go out of your way to pick it up, and you're perfectly good at combat without it. It's balanced and thematic, and if you don't like using it then don't use it.<br /> <br /> If you want to house-rule it off your table, then have fun with that. But every play-style that you personally don't like is not a problem with the rules set.<br /> <br /> I like the preternatural swordfighter who leaps forward, slashes once and sheaves her sword as her opponent falls.<br /> <br /> But then I also like the rising drama of back-to-back challenges, the thrill of escaping the Wyld Hunt and Guild assassins, I like fighting groups of powerful enemies whilst outnumbered, I like epic battles against mile high super-enemies. And I like the dramatic fallout of what happens after the battle: the social and emotional concequences.<br /> <br /> If you're spending two full Excellencies and TAP each combat to kill someone in one blow... what's happening next? Because in my games, you are now sitting at 3i with two opponents left to kill, the world now knows you are Anathema, and once you've killed those opponents you've still got a full day of physical, social and mental challenges ahead. Not to mention what happens tomorrow as various characters swear revenge from the shadows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372209#post1372209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This cannot be stated enough. Combat is this sort of black hole of gameplay where somehow every session end up being at least 50% combat and every combat is critical. <br /> I tried, exactly once, making a character who wasn't good at combat for a &quot;high intrigue low combat&quot; game at the GM's recommendation. It did indeed have less combat, but I walked out halfway through the second session's second fight. It was a horrible slog to sit around doing nothing meaningful except almost dying because I didn't build a murderhobo. <br /> <br /> EVERY other subsystem can be worked around, roleplayed around, the works. You can build a ship, steal a ship, buy a ship, get a pirate to let you ride his ship, conjure a cloud-chariot, etc, or even just give up and decide you don't want to cross that ocean. But nope, gotta fight those fights no alternatives allowed except character death.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1998 I played a lesbian character in order to explore some LGBT issues. The ST was a massive homophobe and until today, pulling out the details of that gruesome game was my number 1 example of &quot;how to ST wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why, WHY, can't you hire mercenaries? Talk your way out of problems? Speed away on the back of a Stormwind Rider? Hide? Flood your enemies in Blood Apes? Narrate combat dramatically? Use the Resolving Battles sidebar on page 205? Use the Skip It sidebar on page 212? Take a Crippling Injury to avoid death? Get captured and play an exciting break-out scene? Use magic to banish spirits? Turn Immaterial and float away? Use the Twilight Anima power? Travel Without Distance? Use a Working to turn your blood into poisonous scorpions so your foes are hesitant to attack you? Just not have any combat and stick to the Session 0 expectations of the game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372209#post1372209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too find it absurd that TTRPGs seem utterly terrified of a seasoned warrior having the slightest clue about the capabilities of his opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default stats for all the Antagonists, including the levels of capability for all Quick Characters, is explicitly laid out in the Corebook. This isn't Paranoia. The players are allowed to know how the game works.<br /> <br /> All Charms have to be declared. Anima gives a visual representation of power use.<br /> <br /> I'll grant you that you're not beginning every combat with a Profile Character, but Measure the Wind exists even if your ST hates you and refuses to play to the spirit of Exalted's system transparency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st Edition Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Have Fun:</b> This suggestion is even more important than the golden rule. If nobody is having fun there's no reason to continue the game. If you're happy with the way your game is going then nobody - not us, not gaming magazines, not other gamers on the internet - can tell you that the way you are playing is &quot;wrong&quot;, as long as you're having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>really</b> don't like telling people they're playing wrong. But if you're not <i>having fun</i> then you're playing wrong.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a system problem. I think this is a story and playstyle problem -- but it's not my problem. I want to help y'all enjoy Exalted more, not tell you off for playing in a way I don't like -- and I realize I've spent the better part of two threads arguing with people who say this is a problem for them. Well, I've said my piece and I'm not going to respond to anyone who doesn't directly ask me a question.<br /> <br /> But I am curious about what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> said: if you think this is a problem, I'd really like to read about what you're doing to fix it. How are you changing the system to make it closer to your expectations? What do you guys think is the solution here?<br /> <br /> I've seen adding more dice to combatants to make them more powerful. Anything else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-02-2020, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T01:39:09-08:00","id":1372234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372232#post1372232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I am curious about what Chausse said: if you think this is a problem, I'd really like to read about what you're doing to fix it. How are you changing the system to make it closer to your expectations? What do you guys think is the solution here?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the solution is not running this system. Half of my six person group has shitlisted it and won't touch it again. One dropped after a social encounter where the PCs were flailing around not accomplishing anything (<i>probably because none of them had read the social rules despite last session ending on an impending-social-encounter cliffhanger</i>) and walked out having had to make a Eclipse-deal with an Abyssal that they wouldn't interfere with the siege of Thorns. The other dropped after a 4 Solar v 3 DB + Size 3 Troops encounter ate six hours realtime and half the Solars might as well have sat the fight out or ran after the mooks dropped. Once again I blame players not knowing how to play, individual character-turns were taking upwards of five minutes per and two of them sat on 20+ Init for multiple turns until I prodded them to Decisive already. <br /> I had no clue what the fuck to do to make Exalted work. I tried a run-away-from-Immaculates starter session. It seemed to go well but there was a clear undercurrent of &quot;When do we stop running?&quot;. I tried an open ended session with a bit of fight and a bit of talk and a bit of research. The Circle tried to go three different ways at once. I tried a talky session. I lost a player. I tried a fighty session. I lost another player and the game died. <br /> I can trace a bunch of these problems to EX3 being a system where you can't &quot;learn as you play&quot; but I can also trace them to the players throwing together vaguely coherent piles of dots and Charms at chargen. Two of the five Solars had no place in a fight, but one of others was a nigh-invincible wargod. Three of the five Solars had no place in a social scene. On and on like this, with nothing to tie the Circle together as &quot;We can all enjoy a scene of X&quot; for <i>any X</i> other than &quot;roleplaying without dice&quot;. <br /> Sure, I could have prevented this if I'd known it was a problem I might encounter. I didn't. I was coming in totally fresh, zero Exalted experience aside from reading a story somebody posted on /tg/. My players enjoyed Tomb of Dreams, progressed into chargen, and I don't think the game actually survived contact with players making characters. I think I just saw a corpse twitching for a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T02:02:01-08:00","id":1372236,"title":"","content":"Well... I guess that's what Exalted: Essence is for.<br /> Or, like, practice games with mortals? <br /> <br /> <br /> Because I guess that, considering you pick 15 different powers at character gen, if people don't read the rules properly (partly their fault, but bloody hell the Corebook is huge) then I can see that it's easy to go wrong.<br /> Certainly, I have seen the least-mechanically minded of our playgroup get into trouble due to making characters poorly, in a way that with DnD doesn't happen so much.<br /> <br /> Back to optimisation, I solved the issue by running a Lunars-only game. And a ton of experience running Exalted, which I guess new STs just don't have. I always think STing chapters are a waste of time, but new 3rd ed STs really probably could do with serious discussions about power level.<br /> <br /> As to how to solve weak antagonists... I don't really want wolves to get more dice and challenge Dawns. I want more giant demon horrors from beyond reality that only the world's greatest warriors can battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T02:43:33-08:00","id":1372238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372232#post1372232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b>really</b> don't like telling people they're playing wrong. But if you're not <i>having fun</i> then you're playing wrong.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a system problem. I think this is a story and playstyle problem -- but it's not my problem. I want to help y'all enjoy Exalted more, not tell you off for playing in a way I don't like -- and I realize I've spent the better part of two threads arguing with people who say this is a problem for them. Well, I've said my piece and I'm not going to respond to anyone who doesn't directly ask me a question.<br /> <br /> But I am curious about what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> said: if you think this is a problem, I'd really like to read about what you're doing to fix it. How are you changing the system to make it closer to your expectations? What do you guys think is the solution here?<br /> <br /> I've seen adding more dice to combatants to make them more powerful. Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make a more exhaustive answer later, but I think it's important to underline that I'm having fun. It's like cooking a very good dinner but you didn't season all your meals the way you intended to. It doesn't mean it's bad or that I don't like it, I usually enjoy it because I love eating, but I'm still taking notes and trying to find ideas for later because next time I want to change a specific part of the experience.<br /> <br /> If I didn't have fun with Exalted I wouldn't be posting on this forum. I've had terrible experiences on Exalted but I think they were more on my account or on the players that didn't act in good faith, or didn't try to adapt and stayed too rigid when taken by surprise. There are of course parts of the system that I think are flawed, but I'm okay with it. I prefer a game with problems that does something I like very much like Exalted better than a perfect game made with total minutiae that stays in a territory I find boring (like a lot of the D&amp;Ds).<br /> <br /> Also, vwllss trnt prncss, I'm sorry for your experience, I understand how frustrating it can be. My first game as a ST had a player that didn't read English very well and for this player it was very difficult to make the game run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T04:16:30-08:00","id":1372245,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> So I'm not sure what &quot;problem&quot; exactly you are talking about, because the topic is very broad. Could you narrow it a bit and precise your question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:34:46-08:00","id":1372270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372245#post1372245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> So I'm not sure what &quot;problem&quot; exactly you are talking about, because the topic is very broad. Could you narrow it a bit and precise your question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the &quot;problem&quot; is finding the Exalted combat system boring.<br /> <br /> I don't have that problem, I think it's super-amazing cool. Easily the best combat system Exalted has ever had.<br /> <br /> But people say it's boring and repetative and they want epic battles and not to win with nova strikes.<br /> <br /> You can pick up the start of the conversation: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370624#post1370624\">here</a>.<br /> And a saliant description of the &quot;problem&quot;: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370842#post1370842\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:39:59-08:00","id":1372272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372232#post1372232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <b>really</b> don't like telling people they're playing wrong. But if you're not <i>having fun</i> then you're playing wrong.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a system problem. I think this is a story and playstyle problem -- but it's not my problem. I want to help y'all enjoy Exalted more, not tell you off for playing in a way I don't like -- and I realize I've spent the better part of two threads arguing with people who say this is a problem for them. Well, I've said my piece and I'm not going to respond to anyone who doesn't directly ask me a question.<br /> <br /> But I am curious about what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> said: if you think this is a problem, I'd really like to read about what you're doing to fix it. How are you changing the system to make it closer to your expectations? What do you guys think is the solution here?<br /> <br /> I've seen adding more dice to combatants to make them more powerful. Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a direct question for you - although feel free not to answer it if you don't think you would enjoy it, as it could also be a question for other people in this thread too.<br /> <br /> I would like to have combat with dramatic back and forth struggle. Instead, combat in my current games against powerful opponents can get long, slow, and repetitive when we don't develop a crushing advantage in the first few turns. Do you have advice, for me or the ST, that might help with this?<br /> <br /> More specifically we are two high Essence Solars - a Night Caste who uses Brawl, Stealth, and Dodge charms in combat, and a Twilight Caste who uses Melee charms and spells in combat. Most of our combat is against Dragonbloodeds (with some Sidereals, mortals, and battlegroups thrown in), because we are fighting the Realm. <br /> <br /> The problem seems to be caused primarily by the combination of my strong defensive charms (Dipping Swallow Defense + Fivefold Bulwark Stance + War Lion Stance + Hail-Shattering Practice is a powerful combination) and Falling Hammer Strike. These Charms are very mote-efficient, so if we are outnumbered, defeat one or two of the enemies but then find ourselves low on motes, we can shut down the enemy's attacks and slowly build up onslaught for a powerful attack. However, this can get very boring as it involves repeating the same actions for many turns. If instead, because of this, we try to get aggressive when low on motes, it often goes quite badly, as it takes a lot of motes to put together an effective attack against a DB in heavy jade armor, and it can still easily fail or not do much damage.<br /> <br /> Do you think we should just get more aggressive Charms (or spells)? Should we play differently? Should our Storyteller put us against somewhat different enemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:27:51-08:00","id":1372280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372272#post1372272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a direct question for you - although feel free not to answer it if you don't think you would enjoy it, as it could also be a question for other people in this thread too.<br /> <br /> I would like to have combat with dramatic back and forth struggle. Instead, combat in my current games against powerful opponents can get long, slow, and repetitive when we don't develop a crushing advantage in the first few turns. Do you have advice, for me or the ST, that might help with this?<br /> <br /> More specifically we are two high Essence Solars - a Night Caste who uses Brawl, Stealth, and Dodge charms in combat, and a Twilight Caste who uses Melee charms and spells in combat. Most of our combat is against Dragonbloodeds (with some Sidereals, mortals, and battlegroups thrown in), because we are fighting the Realm.<br /> <br /> The problem seems to be caused primarily by the combination of my strong defensive charms (Dipping Swallow Defense + Fivefold Bulwark Stance + War Lion Stance + Hail-Shattering Practice is a powerful combination) and Falling Hammer Strike. These Charms are very mote-efficient, so if we are outnumbered, defeat one or two of the enemies but then find ourselves low on motes, we can shut down the enemy's attacks and slowly build up onslaught for a powerful attack. However, this can get very boring as it involves repeating the same actions for many turns. If instead, because of this, we try to get aggressive when low on motes, it often goes quite badly, as it takes a lot of motes to put together an effective attack against a DB in heavy jade armor, and it can still easily fail or not do much damage.<br /> <br /> Do you think we should just get more aggressive Charms (or spells)? Should we play differently? Should our Storyteller put us against somewhat different enemies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, happy to help.<br /> <br /> High Essence Solars are beasts. In the arena thread we've pit starting Solars against Essence 5 Deebs and the Solars have won. But sure, let's see what we can do, eh?<br /> <br /> Strong Defensive Charms: Fivefold Bulwark Stance+Hail Shattering Practice is the Deeb killer, no doubt about it. Cancel out most penalities, and rest on a Defense of 7 which you can top up to 8 with 1m then boost after the fact with 1s.<br /> <br /> Multiple opponents still help. A 16d attack might roll an average of 8 successes (and get Hail Shattered into a miss), but the more times you roll, the more likely you are to roll above average. I'd be looking at 3 Experienced Dragon-Blooded (Corebook p544) per Solar. A Size 1 Battlegroup of Blood Apes shouldn't be beyond the Dynasty's ability to throw out.<br /> <br /> But, now we're into that long mote slog, kill one then slowly, painstakingly build higher or die.<br /> <br /> Let's address that mote rebuild. White Reaper cancels Onslaught and makes them a defensive bonus. No reason why your Dragon-Blooded shouldn't have the ability to shut down Falling Hammer Strike now and then. Take a look at some of the other Martial Arts whilst you're there: Deebs have access to a lot of Onslaught negation if you go looking for it.<br /> <br /> We're now in a position where you can't instantly win, the enemies have real chance of hitting you, and your mote rebuilding by stacking endless Onslaught has been negated... but if anything we just made the fight longer.<br /> <br /> So what should you do?<br /> <br /> You said you were high Essence. Lore has Power-Restoring Invocation and Surging Inner Fire for restoring motes quickly. The downside is, this is costing you your action... which, for you, is an upside. The Deebs all get a free round of attacks on you which might Crash you, but you get your motes back so you can act quicker.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the enemy's actions might help. Grapples can reliably be pulled off with 6i. Disarms at 7i: Table Turning Reversal can be purchased by a starting Deeb.<br /> <br /> War Lion stance is great... for the ST. Everyone hates escort missions, and even if you are tough, your allies aren't as tough.<br /> <br /> Orders given to battlegroups of mortal archers sitting at Long range can be deadly.<br /> <br /> For playing more aggressively, Heaven Sword Flash and Thunderbolt Attack Prana can kill very deadly foes very quickly. You might not get that dramatic back and forth... but then, maybe you might? Kill three Dragon-Blooded on turn 1, then have two Sidereal assassins pop out once you're low on motes.<br /> <br /> But also... This is kinda intended?<br /> <br /> Heavy Armor is meant to help keep you alive in combat. Solars are meant to be more powerful than Dragon-Blooded. When outnumbered, Solars need to fight conservatively to avoid being overwhelmed. Your very powerful, high essence characters are very powerful.<br /> <br /> Have you considered not fighting the Realm?<br /> <br /> Maybe have the rumour of a weapon that could help you defeat the Realm take you away from the main campaign and give you an excuse to fight mile high volcano monsters, second circle demons and Lunar elders?<br /> <br /> Fighting the Realm is always going to be a long, slow, slog. You're two people against a world-spanning empire that's going to fight you for every inch of ground. There isn't going to be a dramatic reversal where you drop the Realm to its knees in one blow, before they reveal that they're not left-handed. At least, not setting as written.<br /> <br /> I don't want combat with a lot of back-and-forth-struggle. I call that &quot;swing&quot;, and it's explicitly not fun for me.<br /> <br /> That's different from dramatic combat. I love dramatic combat.<br /> <br /> When you watch an action movie, do you really, honestly believe that the protagonist is going to get killed by some random mook who hasn't even got a name tag?<br /> <br /> Killing three random quick characters is not dramatic. Even if you have five Initative Shifts over the course of the combat.<br /> Fights are dramatic when there's meaning and concequence behind them.<br /> <br /> But, if you want to recapture the feel of iconic fights (like Rugen vs Montoya or Edmund vs Dantes) then NPCs opening with a Decisive, Stunted, Willpower backed, Full Excellency can provide some of that swing. Putting wound penalities on you, and making them vulnerable to Crash (potentially opening the chance for a Shift).<br /> <br /> To answer your questions:<br /> <br /> Do you think we should just get more aggressive Charms (or spells)?<br /> <br /> That alone is unlikely to give you dramatic back and forth. But it can help with building up motes, and if you move to starting every fight with something like Iron Whirlwind Attack to put wound penalties on all your opponents at risk of them Crashing you, then that might help. Look at some of the &quot;interesting&quot; Brawl charms I posted. Collapsing the building you are fighting in might not help win your fights faster, but it might add the element of drama you are looking for.<br /> <br /> Should we play differently?<br /> <br /> Honestly? You'd have more fun with weaker characters. Why not make a couple of suboptimal Dynasts and play two or three sessions to see how the other-half lives. For example, if you recently liberated a kingdom from the Realm and moved on, your new characters could try and retake that kingdom. If you don't enjoy playing a Dragon-Blooded, then you can go back to playing Solars and go free the kingdom again -- and you haven't &quot;wasted&quot; any time then, you've just set up the next chapter of your on-going Solar game.<br /> <br /> (Did you enjoy my fight between Sugar Daddy Captain and the Manticore? That's what low level combat looks like.)<br /> <br /> Should our Storyteller put us against somewhat different enemies?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that'd help. DrLoveMonkey has some good NPC advice in the Arena thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-02-2020, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T10:08:30-08:00","id":1372297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372272#post1372272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think we should just get more aggressive Charms (or spells)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well with only two characters, it's hard to tell. A Solar with Melee can absolutely kill 5 dragonblooded in a single turn using a combination of effects. One that's so good I'm probably going to take it out of any of my Arena fights and disallow it at my table is Divine Executioner Stance, which if you take a definite principle of hatred for all those who dare oppose you is just +4 to attack and damage, even decisive damage, for just 1m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372272#post1372272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we play differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably just playing how the combats are forcing you to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372272#post1372272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should our Storyteller put us against somewhat different enemies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly. A lot of Storytellers or Dungeonmasters get mad when their big epic combats get destroyed in one turn by Invincible Fury of the Dawn/Fireball/Meteor Swarm, and in response they make the next combat even awesomer and more deadly, and then it gets destroyed in one turn by Heaven Sword Flash/Meteor Swarm, and so they make the next try EVEN CRAZIER, until eventually you're fighting some dude with 40 soak or 1,500hp or something and that one combat takes 6 hours and nobody really feels awesome.<br /> <br /> What to do instead is to realize that as the ST your resources to put obstacles in front of the PCs are effectively limitless depending on how much BS you want to make up, and considering that Exalted is an epic fantasy world of high fantasy and over-the-top places/people you don't really have to stretch it too far. The storms in Creation are more powerful and more frequent than storms on Earth, there are legions of magically enhanced ogre-soldiers, there are superhumans born of one woman and ten fathers, the seas hide the nations of monsterous and beautiful aquatic civilizations.<br /> <br /> The PCs like to feel awesome though, and most STs like their PCs to feel awesome. So break up combat encounters into 3-5 medium difficulty ones. That way the players can use their epic superhero powers to smash through things and actually <i>feel </i>like superheroes, but also keep challenge into it because eventually everyone runs out of motes. With only 2 PCs that should be a piece of cake. A size 1 battlegroup isn't just easy for the Realm to field, it's easy for just one sorcerer to field, a size 2-3 battlegroup of bloodapes isn't even out of the question for the realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also JohnDoe is right about the Realm, it's really, really big. Apparently it has ~500 kingdoms that call themselves satrapies alone, nevermind the Isle itself. Just two Solars aren't really likely to bring it down on their own unless maybe they take control of the Sword of Creation or something similar. Which you can do, the Empress did it and it seemed to work out for her. You might want to try circumnavigating Creation uniting recently returned Solars with Lunars and making sure they don't kill eachother, while doing the opposite and fanning the civil war flames one the Blessed Isle if you were going to do that.<br /> <br /> Or you can make a campaign about freeing a satrapy or two and that's just fine. Some satrapies were made by taking over another empire and breaking it apart into several nations, so freeing them all and reuniting the Empire of Fariou or something could be pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T10:44:49-08:00","id":1372301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372234#post1372234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -snip-</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) This is one of the issues with the E3 system. Its <i><b>complicated as fuck</b></i>, and you have to understand what is going on before hand. <br /> <br /> 2) Another issue is that Exalted, at least E3, largely lacks a &quot;Dungeon Master's Guide&quot;. Creating <i><b>and balancing</b></i> a game, session or even encounter for Exalted is really quite difficult, especially when your players can run the gamut from &quot;God of War&quot; to 'Social Mastermind&quot;. Adding in Charms doesn't help much.<br /> <br /> I, personally, have found that many of these issues are lessened through playing Mortals instead of Exalted. Mortals are easier to build, easier to balance, and easier to play than Exalted. It might not be what some people here like to hear, but I (and my players) have found that E3-but-with-Mortals is <i><b>much</b></i> more enjoyable than with Exalted. <br /> <br /> Humbly, I suggest you give it a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T11:17:16-08:00","id":1372305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372297#post1372297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with only two characters, it's hard to tell. A Solar with Melee can absolutely kill 5 dragonblooded in a single turn using a combination of effects. One that's so good I'm probably going to take it out of any of my Arena fights and disallow it at my table is Divine Executioner Stance, which if you take a definite principle of hatred for all those who dare oppose you is just +4 to attack and damage, even decisive damage, for just 1m.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're probably just playing how the combats are forcing you to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Almost certainly. A lot of Storytellers or Dungeonmasters get mad when their big epic combats get destroyed in one turn by Invincible Fury of the Dawn/Fireball/Meteor Swarm, and in response they make the next combat even awesomer and more deadly, and then it gets destroyed in one turn by Heaven Sword Flash/Meteor Swarm, and so they make the next try EVEN CRAZIER, until eventually you're fighting some dude with 40 soak or 1,500hp or something and that one combat takes 6 hours and nobody really feels awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the detailed reply!<br /> <br /> I don't actually have Heaven Sword Flash, nor even very much of its prerequisite tree, though I will probably go some portion of the way down it next. I don't want to solve the issue of combats taking too long by making them take 1 turn, but I think as long as I try to conserve my Willpower and don't combine Thunderbolt Attack Prana with a million other charms, that would be fine.<br /> <br /> But it's definitely true there's been an escalation over time between players and ST. (Which is fine - I do certainly want some challenge).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What to do instead is to realize that as the ST your resources to put obstacles in front of the PCs are effectively limitless depending on how much BS you want to make up, and considering that Exalted is an epic fantasy world of high fantasy and over-the-top places/people you don't really have to stretch it too far. The storms in Creation are more powerful and more frequent than storms on Earth, there are legions of magically enhanced ogre-soldiers, there are superhumans born of one woman and ten fathers, the seas hide the nations of monsterous and beautiful aquatic civilizations.<br /> <br /> The PCs like to feel awesome though, and most STs like their PCs to feel awesome. So break up combat encounters into 3-5 medium difficulty ones. That way the players can use their epic superhero powers to smash through things and actually <i>feel </i>like superheroes, but also keep challenge into it because eventually everyone runs out of motes. With only 2 PCs that should be a piece of cake. A size 1 battlegroup isn't just easy for the Realm to field, it's easy for just one sorcerer to field, a size 2-3 battlegroup of bloodapes isn't even out of the question for the realm. </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense! This might be a bit tricky to implement on some of the adventures we typically go on, as with a Night caste and another solar with ranks in Stealth, we usually try to sneak into the satrap's palace (or similar locales) and fight them directly, rather than going through their guards first. This does lower our mote pools a bit but doesn't always lead to us feeling as badass (in particular making one or two bad rolls can be more awkward-feeling in Stealth than in combat). But I'm sure there are still ways to apply this strategy, and anyways we probably won't end up trying the same exact thing next time (at the very least, we'll try to bluff our way in). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also JohnDoe is right about the Realm, it's really, really big. Apparently it has ~500 kingdoms that call themselves satrapies alone, nevermind the Isle itself. Just two Solars aren't really likely to bring it down on their own unless maybe they take control of the Sword of Creation or something similar. Which you can do, the Empress did it and it seemed to work out for her. You might want to try circumnavigating Creation uniting recently returned Solars with Lunars and making sure they don't kill eachother, while doing the opposite and fanning the civil war flames one the Blessed Isle if you were going to do that.<br /> <br /> Or you can make a campaign about freeing a satrapy or two and that's just fine. Some satrapies were made by taking over another empire and breaking it apart into several nations, so freeing them all and reuniting the Empire of Fariou or something could be pretty cool. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could have been more specific - freeing a satrapy or two is exactly what we're doing. (We killed or forced to flee the defenders of one so far, but they will be back with more legions and more DBs, so we're gathering strength to face them, which I can neither confirm or deny involve sabotaging one of the neighboring satrapies). We're not trying to kill 10,000 dragonblooded one by one. But we do get into fights with 3+ dragonbloodeds at a time pretty regularly.<br /> <br /> But we will probably end up in some fights against other foes soon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 03-02-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T11:53:13-08:00","id":1372310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372280#post1372280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want combat with a lot of back-and-forth-struggle. I call that &quot;swing&quot;, and it's explicitly not fun for me.<br /> <br /> That's different from dramatic combat. I love dramatic combat.<br /> <br /> When you watch an action movie, do you really, honestly believe that the protagonist is going to get killed by some random mook who hasn't even got a name tag?<br /> <br /> Killing three random quick characters is not dramatic. Even if you have five Initative Shifts over the course of the combat.<br /> Fights are dramatic when there's meaning and concequence behind them.<br /> <br /> But, if you want to recapture the feel of iconic fights (like Rugen vs Montoya or Edmund vs Dantes) then NPCs opening with a Decisive, Stunted, Willpower backed, Full Excellency can provide some of that swing. Putting wound penalities on you, and making them vulnerable to Crash (potentially opening the chance for a Shift).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your detailed reply, and especially for this bit.<br /> <br /> It made me think about what I really want out of combat (and combat systems).<br /> <br /> I agree that the most important aspect of the combat is the narrative. But on a purely mechanical level, I think the ideal combat for me is not super swingy. Instead what I like is (1) getting to use a few different cool powers on a few different turns and (2) getting to make interesting strategic decisions. <br /> <br /> So ideally I would like enemies to be powerful enough that it's worth spending motes on Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike and Hungry Tiger Technique and Dipping Swallow Defense and such, and powerful enough that I don't kill them in one turn by spending motes on those things, but not so powerful that I feel like I'm wasting motes when I've spent them on those things as they easily defend or absorb the attack.<br /> <br /> But I don't particularly enjoy the feeling of expecting to lose at one point in the combat and expecting to win at another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, happy to help.<br /> <br /> High Essence Solars are beasts. In the arena thread we've pit starting Solars against Essence 5 Deebs and the Solars have won. But sure, let's see what we can do, eh?<br /> <br /> Strong Defensive Charms: Fivefold Bulwark Stance+Hail Shattering Practice is the Deeb killer, no doubt about it. Cancel out most penalities, and rest on a Defense of 7 which you can top up to 8 with 1m then boost after the fact with 1s.<br /> <br /> Multiple opponents still help. A 16d attack might roll an average of 8 successes (and get Hail Shattered into a miss), but the more times you roll, the more likely you are to roll above average. I'd be looking at 3 Experienced Dragon-Blooded (Corebook p544) per Solar. A Size 1 Battlegroup of Blood Apes shouldn't be beyond the Dynasty's ability to throw out.<br /> <br /> But, now we're into that long mote slog, kill one then slowly, painstakingly build higher or die.<br /> <br /> Let's address that mote rebuild. White Reaper cancels Onslaught and makes them a defensive bonus. No reason why your Dragon-Blooded shouldn't have the ability to shut down Falling Hammer Strike now and then. Take a look at some of the other Martial Arts whilst you're there: Deebs have access to a lot of Onslaught negation if you go looking for it.<br /> <br /> We're now in a position where you can't instantly win, the enemies have real chance of hitting you, and your mote rebuilding by stacking endless Onslaught has been negated... but if anything we just made the fight longer.<br /> <br /> So what should you do?<br /> <br /> You said you were high Essence. Lore has Power-Restoring Invocation and Surging Inner Fire for restoring motes quickly. The downside is, this is costing you your action... which, for you, is an upside. The Deebs all get a free round of attacks on you which might Crash you, but you get your motes back so you can act quicker. </div> </div> </div>Cool - despite having a bunch of Lore charms I'm actually far from that tree, because the beginning charms in it didn't seem that fun, but I'll check it out and see if it's worth investing in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also feel like the enemy's actions might help. Grapples can reliably be pulled off with 6i. Disarms at 7i: Table Turning Reversal can be purchased by a starting Deeb.<br /> <br /> War Lion stance is great... for the ST. Everyone hates escort missions, and even if you are tough, your allies aren't as tough. </div> </div> </div>This is a good idea, and in particular should bring the narrative and the combat gameplay closer together, which I like. It almost happened in the campaign but then the enemies had to run away due to the (somewhat Heaven Sword Flash-like) powers of our dragon ally, so our weaker allies weren't particularly threatened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Orders given to battlegroups of mortal archers sitting at Long range can be deadly. </div> </div> </div>And attacking battlegroups of mortals is generally pretty fun as they have low defenses and withering damage has a direct impact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For playing more aggressively, Heaven Sword Flash and Thunderbolt Attack Prana can kill very deadly foes very quickly. You might not get that dramatic back and forth... but then, maybe you might? Kill three Dragon-Blooded on turn 1, then have two Sidereal assassins pop out once you're low on motes.<br /> <br /> But also... This is kinda intended?<br /> <br /> Heavy Armor is meant to help keep you alive in combat. Solars are meant to be more powerful than Dragon-Blooded. When outnumbered, Solars need to fight conservatively to avoid being overwhelmed. Your very powerful, high essence characters are very powerful. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fair. In part I'm just complaining because a confluence of predictable and unpredictable factors led us into a situation where we had to fight very, very conservatively. Like, I took the Full Defense action on multiple turns, and I'm pretty sure it was the right tactical call. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you considered not fighting the Realm?<br /> <br /> Maybe have the rumour of a weapon that could help you defeat the Realm take you away from the main campaign and give you an excuse to fight mile high volcano monsters, second circle demons and Lunar elders? </div> </div> </div>This is a good idea and certainly something I want to try next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fighting the Realm is always going to be a long, slow, slog. You're two people against a world-spanning empire that's going to fight you for every inch of ground. There isn't going to be a dramatic reversal where you drop the Realm to its knees in one blow, before they reveal that they're not left-handed. At least, not setting as written.<br /> <br /> <br /> To answer your questions:<br /> <br /> Do you think we should just get more aggressive Charms (or spells)?<br /> <br /> That alone is unlikely to give you dramatic back and forth. But it can help with building up motes, and if you move to starting every fight with something like Iron Whirlwind Attack to put wound penalties on all your opponents at risk of them Crashing you, then that might help. Look at some of the &quot;interesting&quot; Brawl charms I posted. Collapsing the building you are fighting in might not help win your fights faster, but it might add the element of drama you are looking for.<br /> <br /> Should we play differently?<br /> <br /> Honestly? You'd have more fun with weaker characters. Why not make a couple of suboptimal Dynasts and play two or three sessions to see how the other-half lives. For example, if you recently liberated a kingdom from the Realm and moved on, your new characters could try and retake that kingdom. If you don't enjoy playing a Dragon-Blooded, then you can go back to playing Solars and go free the kingdom again -- and you haven't &quot;wasted&quot; any time then, you've just set up the next chapter of your on-going Solar game. </div> </div> </div>Oh this is a really interesting idea. That's not quite where we are but I'll think if there's a way to incorporate it into our game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T12:34:41-08:00","id":1372316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372305#post1372305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes a lot of sense! This might be a bit tricky to implement on some of the adventures we typically go on, as with a Night caste and another solar with ranks in Stealth, we usually try to sneak into the satrap's palace (or similar locales) and fight them directly, rather than going through their guards first. This does lower our mote pools a bit but doesn't always lead to us feeling as badass (in particular making one or two bad rolls can be more awkward-feeling in Stealth than in combat). But I'm sure there are still ways to apply this strategy, and anyways we probably won't end up trying the same exact thing next time (at the very least, we'll try to bluff our way in).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to give this some thought and get back to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also something else I've noticed from my experience, especially with the Arena, is that foes that have high defense and high soak fighting eachother is a bloody slog. It takes forever, hours and hours, one combat could take more than an entire session easily. It sucks, it's clearly not what the system was designed to do, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372301#post1372301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, have found that many of these issues are lessened through playing Mortals instead of Exalted. Mortals are easier to build, easier to balance, and easier to play than Exalted. It might not be what some people here like to hear, but I (and my players) have found that E3-but-with-Mortals is <i><b>much</b></i> more enjoyable than with Exalted.<br /> <br /> Humbly, I suggest you give it a shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can second this. Out of the half dozen ex3 campaigns I've been involved with the most consistently fun one was the mortals one. I've had lots of fun with all of them, but I basically didn't have any bad times with the mortals one. We battled entire armies with just four of us, we killed exalted warriors, we traveled to the edges of the world and fought horrors beyond time and space. It was pretty sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T18:00:15-08:00","id":1372358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372316#post1372316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll try to give this some thought and get back to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! It's totally fine if you don't though - I'm not the ST so I can't say for certain how helpful your advice will be to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also something else I've noticed from my experience, especially with the Arena, is that foes that have high defense and high soak fighting eachother is a bloody slog. It takes forever, hours and hours, one combat could take more than an entire session easily. It sucks, it's clearly not what the system was designed to do, in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>That sounds very plausible to me based on my experience as well. It's kind of funny since Solars vs. DBs is a big theme of the setting, as are other Exalt vs. Exalt pairings, and a lot of those will typically lead to high Defense and/or Soak, but I understand that systems can't be good at anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can second this. Out of the half dozen ex3 campaigns I've been involved with the most consistently fun one was the mortals one. I've had lots of fun with all of them, but I basically didn't have any bad times with the mortals one. We battled entire armies with just four of us, we killed exalted warriors, we traveled to the edges of the world and fought horrors beyond time and space. It was pretty sweet. </div> </div> </div>I would be really interested in hearing more about this! Did you write about this anywhere on the forum? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372301#post1372301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, have found that many of these issues are lessened through playing Mortals instead of Exalted. Mortals are easier to build, easier to balance, and easier to play than Exalted. It might not be what some people here like to hear, but I (and my players) have found that E3-but-with-Mortals is <i><b>much</b></i> more enjoyable than with Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for you - I would be interested to hear about the premise of the game and what happened in it. <br /> <br /> Maybe we could discuss this in another thread, as it may be a bit off topic for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T01:11:11-08:00","id":1372396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372270#post1372270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the &quot;problem&quot; is finding the Exalted combat system boring.<br /> <br /> I don't have that problem, I think it's super-amazing cool. Easily the best combat system Exalted has ever had.<br /> <br /> But people say it's boring and repetative and they want epic battles and not to win with nova strikes.<br /> <br /> You can pick up the start of the conversation: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370624#post1370624\">here</a>.<br /> And a saliant description of the &quot;problem&quot;: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370842#post1370842\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1371140#post1371140\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'll give my personal perspectives that are pretty simple about my problem with this game concerning the fighting part. I'll try to cut it in different parts but some are linked to the others I guess. Some are inherent to the game, some not. None of these necessary turned me off the game, but with all of them I had at least one argument with my players because there were no simple middle-ground we could find that felt fair for everyone.<br /> <br /> 1) Not enough tools for the ST. This one is pretty simple, everyone always talks about it, we don't have enough tools for the ST to create and customize fun, personal and challenging enemies for my characters. Hopefully Crucible will answer this. It took me 2 years before I did a challenge that I believe was really entertaining from the &quot;fighting gameplay perspective&quot;, meaning the outcome of the fight was not obvious after the first 2 turns, they possessed a wide range of different abilities that sollicitated many of the characters different skills as well as the creativity of their players, there was different &quot;objectives&quot; and reversals during the fight, and they won as they should but ended up exhausted, with one character death on the last phase. I obviously did some fights that were interesting before this one, but I never found them interesting from the gameplay perspective.<br /> <br /> 2) The system is overall too complex with too many exceptions and subsystems. You obviously get used to it with practice and I'm fine with that on the long term, and I don't consider the basic system is too complex (with Initiative and withering and stuff), but you quickly have a player asking &quot;Can I grapple this guy ?&quot;, &quot;How does mounted work already ?&quot; &quot;Can I use X Charms under Z circumstances ? I'm not sure&quot; &quot;I try to intimidate this Battle Group&quot; and often the ways to handle this are not straightforward.<br /> <br /> 3) Guess this could go into 1) as well but you will often have &quot;I'd like to fight with an Ice elemental to protect me from the lava god, Bob would like to have his blood ape fight with him, and Alice has her battle group of normal human, but she as well trained and convinced a battle group of war ghost to help us so ...&quot; and suddenly you are like 8v5 in a too complex fight to deal with properly. So I ended up applying your advice which is to ignore fighters too weak to participate but then people asked me &quot;What's the use of summoning stuff if I can't use them in fights because they suck&quot; - &quot;Well ...&quot;. Now I'm regrouping all the players summons into a Battle group with stats depending of the quality of the summons but it's not such an easy decision to take.<br /> <br /> 4) I like the Initiative system but there are still things I'm still trying to work out about how I feel about them :<br /> a) Starting initiative can go very high, and not even counting for Charms like TAP things can be very frustrating even for other player that took time to have combat abilities and stuff because someone will basically start the fight by destroying everything, so there was a lot of momentum and setup for everyone and only one person get to do anything. It's obviously linked to 1) because at first you don't have that much defensive tools for your NPC's and cheating doesn't bother me too much as a ST as long as it doesn't negate a player's impact (which it does in this case).<br /> <br /> b) We discuss already how I don't like that the system doesn't discourage going to high initiative because it just delays the inevitable but is a little pointless. I guess you can say &quot;Maybe at this point just let the PC's win&quot; and I'd answer &quot;Yeah or maybe at this point just do a fucking decisive attack because that's the purpose of the system&quot;.<br /> <br /> c) There are some weird interactions with spells (could go into 2) I guess) where some spells consume Initiative, some not, some work on Willpower, some etc ...<br /> <br /> d) I find the game loses in dynamism at a certain level of Soak, and there are some too easy tools to acquire good Soak at start, which will create weird situations when if you try to adapt a bit as a ST to match the Soak of the Soak player you'll end up gaining 20 initiative on anyone else that you attack.<br /> <br /> I may (or not) come with some other points but I guess these are the major ones that bugged me at least once when playing the game, and I found no easy answer where everyone felt it was the fair and good solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 03-03-2020, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T03:02:03-08:00","id":1372410,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> with a lot of stuff. <br /> <br /> 1-ST tools. I don't have nearly enough monsters and enemies with just Core + WFHW. Yes HDNP is out there but i dont wanna buy 30 pdfs one by one to get monsters. There's <i>one</i> premade adventure that I'm aware of, and it's for not-even-starting strength characters. Compared to DnD which has, like, 8. There isn't anything about how to ST or common plots or how to play Dynasts politically. The game is very &quot;here's 600 pages of rules, DIY&quot;<br /> <br /> 2- Same. I need a flowchart to figure out combat, and then we upgraded to <i>another flowchart</i> which I still use, after 2 years and about 25 sessions. Battlegroups especially are hard to use. <br /> <br /> 3- Its so ridiculously easy to acquire battlegroups, followers, bodyguards, demons, etc that each player has effectively 2 characters minimum. My Eclipse has a pirate crew that get a massive Health bonus from sail and war charms, my Twilight has a Survival pumped Otter God (mechanically a River Dragon), My Zenith &quot;just&quot; has a Fire Caste Dynast bodyguard. The Dawn has 3 Tyrant Lizards. THREE. Don't even get me started on all their dumb artifacts which are weird changes to combat. I mean, I love them and I designed half of them, but each one has its own resource to track and shit. <br /> <br /> 4- TAP and others are insanely, over the top good. My Night Caste can and does start combat with 20+ initiative from Stealth and Larceny, and it's impossible to even attack him without two different abilities, so he's free to get to Ini. 40 before nova-ing somebody right to hell. And that's <i>without</i> TAP. High Soak and Hardness also make fights an incredible slog. there's very little you can do to a Resistance/heavy artifact armor user. Brawl Grapple by itself is countered almost entirely by Brawl Grapple and when my Eclipse gets his hands on someone I basically just ask him how he's gonna kill them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T03:18:22-08:00","id":1372415,"title":"","content":"I find battlegroups really easy to use.<br /> <br /> I do agree about PC goons though.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, lastly... I'm glad my players build characters to be good but not amazing at combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T04:10:31-08:00","id":1372421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372415#post1372415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find battlegroups really easy to use.<br /> <br /> I do agree about PC goons though.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, lastly... I'm glad my players build characters to be good but not amazing at combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battle groups are usually good as long as you don't have too many, yeah I'm really glad they went up with this idea it's really good.<br /> <br /> &quot;Goons&quot; as you call them are more problematic to me, and they usually are harder to &quot;dismiss&quot; because usually they feel personal to the character and the player (summoned character, retainer, etc ...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T04:59:34-08:00","id":1372428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you try and find some way to keep the PC's goons out of it, then they'll feel like the ST is taking their stuff.<br /> <br /> I will say battle groups of PC's soldiers tends not to be so bad, as they're quite simple and their boss's action is probably just roll Command. Also, they tend not to last long against Exalted opponents. But stuff like 2nd circle demons is much more awkward.<br /> <br /> Our ST sometimes has players who aren't in the fight play the goons. So for example the Wyld Hunt ambushed our sorceress; that player played his character and Iyutha, I played his familiar and Florivet, another person played Alveua, etc.<br /> I like this (gives you something to do when there's a combat you're not in) but of course that only works when the PCs are split up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T07:29:33-08:00","id":1372453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372410#post1372410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- Its so ridiculously easy to acquire battlegroups, followers, bodyguards, demons, etc that each player has effectively 2 characters minimum. My Eclipse has a pirate crew that get a massive Health bonus from sail and war charms, my Twilight has a Survival pumped Otter God (mechanically a River Dragon), My Zenith &quot;just&quot; has a Fire Caste Dynast bodyguard. The Dawn has 3 Tyrant Lizards</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like something you might just need to talk to your players about. Like if one of your PCs spent every merit point and bonus point into getting a dozen retainers he absolutely can not expect you to run a combat with 12 additional initiative tracks in it. Even if it was balanced having the combat take six times longer is just bad for everyone involved. I\u2019ve had to do stuff like that before and basically just put my foot down about it. <br /> <br /> For example in my DB game I said that there can\u2019t be more than one young terrestrial retainer per PC, and make it clear that even if they have five they won\u2019t all be joining them in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T07:32:29-08:00","id":1372454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372428#post1372428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if you try and find some way to keep the PC's goons out of it, then they'll feel like the ST is taking their stuff.<br /> <br /> I will say battle groups of PC's soldiers tends not to be so bad, as they're quite simple and their boss's action is probably just roll Command. Also, they tend not to last long against Exalted opponents. But stuff like 2nd circle demons is much more awkward.<br /> <br /> Our ST sometimes has players who aren't in the fight play the goons. So for example the Wyld Hunt ambushed our sorceress; that player played his character and Iyutha, I played his familiar and Florivet, another person played Alveua, etc.<br /> I like this (gives you something to do when there's a combat you're not in) but of course that only works when the PCs are split up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the ideas of games like Fate or PbtA games to integrate this kind of &quot;helpful bonuses&quot; in an Aspect or a sort of usable equipment. I don't know to which extent it would be use in Exalted.<br /> <br /> I tried to workout some things and I had a simple idea where if the player had an argument when an enemy NPC is taking an action (running away, attacking someone with a fire spell, etc ...) and the PC prepared something specific for it (an archer retainer that can shoot far, an ice elemental that protects from fire, etc ...), just give (Merit value) Initiative to the player. It uses the already existing abstracted system of initiative (which is good) in a simple and rewarding way for the player that prepared something, without it being a chore to manage as a ST or a player. I'm still trying to figure out how exactly I want this to take part in the narration of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:11:40-08:00","id":1372574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372453#post1372453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like something you might just need to talk to your players about. Like if one of your PCs spent every merit point and bonus point into getting a dozen retainers he absolutely can not expect you to run a combat with 12 additional initiative tracks in it. Even if it was balanced having the combat take six times longer is just bad for everyone involved. I\u2019ve had to do stuff like that before and basically just put my foot down about it.<br /> <br /> For example in my DB game I said that there can\u2019t be more than one young terrestrial retainer per PC, and make it clear that even if they have five they won\u2019t all be joining them in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is inherent to the &quot;any kind of hero&quot; fantasy that Exalted lets people do. My Sail Supernal Eclipse player was <i>ecstatic </i>that he could play an actual pirate, not just a barbarian with an eyepatch. He has a Ship, a Crew, and War Charms. That's not bad. My Twilight players loves otters and bought the 2 dot merit as kind of a joke for fun when he realized he could, but that became an intergral part of his character so much that I let him switch Supernal from Occult to Survival. My Zenith player wanted to play a mad prophet harley quinn as the pope character b/c she's never done roleplaying and really jumped on the idea of &quot;you can play anything&quot; and thats the kind of character she wants to play. She got a young DB bodyguard as both a surrogate little sister and to cover the fact that she doesn't want her character to take fighting charms. One guy is just gonna be here for like 3 sessions and he wants to ride a trex and fight with an ax. <br /> <br /> I can't take those away from my players, they either came about organically or are integral parts of character creation and identity. My Night Larceny Yakuza specifically <i>doesn't</i> want to rebuild his destroyed gang because I as a player don't want <i><b>yet another</b></i> group of extras around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T08:13:43-08:00","id":1373380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1372415#post1372415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find battlegroups really easy to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't personally have any issues with using battle groups.<br /> I do have a minor problem with using them as antagonists, which is that the area attack means we're moving at the speed of the slowest person in the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T08:45:07-08:00","id":1373381,"title":"","content":"Could you expand on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T09:08:20-08:00","id":1373385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1373381#post1373381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you expand on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>An enemy commander orders his battlegroup to attack, and they do, the Dawn activates Dipping Swallow and 4m excellency, but due to the epic command roll the BG just barely hits, the Dawns heavy armor unable to soak away the huge damage still takes 2 initiative damage. The twilight on the other hand is hit by 10 successes, and his 5 soak means he took 12 initiative damage. Next time the BG swings like that it might hit the dawn but will almost certainly slay the twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T09:10:52-08:00","id":1373388,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T10:22:13-08:00","id":1373401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1373385#post1373385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An enemy commander orders his battlegroup to attack, and they do, the Dawn activates Dipping Swallow and 4m excellency, but due to the epic command roll the BG just barely hits, the Dawns heavy armor unable to soak away the huge damage still takes 2 initiative damage. The twilight on the other hand is hit by 10 successes, and his 5 soak means he took 12 initiative damage. Next time the BG swings like that it might hit the dawn but will almost certainly slay the twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Twilight player might have purchased a few combat charms that they lack a quick reference for and they start looking stuff up mid-combat. It's not as bad but can still make you go &quot;jesus christ! this thing was supposed to save us time&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T10:44:58-08:00","id":1373404,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that makes sense too, in my experience everyone has some combat charms at least but the people with the median amount of combat charms know them least well (the Dawn knows them because he cares the most, the ones with least combat charms just have less to know). That may just be my group though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:15:37-08:00","id":1373407,"title":"","content":"In my experience the weakpoint tends to be where the charms existed slightly differently in previous editions.<br /> <br /> For example: Most people I've encountered recall Dipping Swallow is instant, Bulwark Stance is a turn and Fivefold Bulwark Stance is a scene because in 1st and 2nd edition the latter made the two before it pretty obsolete but fewer remember that Dipping Swallow now gives +1i if you defend successfully and Bulwark Stance reduces the damage roll for every 1 on the attack roll and in a scenario like what DrLoveMonkey described knowing about that aspect of Bulwark Stance is potentially character life or death.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T14:32:34-08:00","id":1373436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1373404#post1373404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that makes sense too, in my experience everyone has some combat charms at least but the people with the median amount of combat charms know them least well (the Dawn knows them because he cares the most, the ones with least combat charms just have less to know). That may just be my group though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems like another reason to have the group at session 0 agree to take a smaller-than-normal number of combat charms, so hopefully everyone has an amount they can remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:20:48-07:00","id":1396347,"title":"","content":"Exalted 3e combat is, weird and abstract you can basically bring a defense 1 1 health level creature and with a melee artifact weapon withering attack it to get all the initiative you need have the non combat person in your party decisive it to kill it off so your enemy doesnt do the same then toss a pebble as a decisive and somehow one shot them while the non combat lore supernal is under the dawns protective cares of your parry fills up the dawns essence pool so you come out mote positive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T05:22:10-07:00","id":1396360,"title":"","content":"Umm, what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T06:19:10-07:00","id":1396365,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I didn't really follow that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:14:34-07:00","id":1396388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396347#post1396347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted 3e combat is, weird and abstract you can basically bring a defense 1 1 health level creature and with a melee artifact weapon withering attack it to get all the initiative you need have the non combat person in your party decisive it to kill it off so your enemy doesnt do the same then toss a pebble as a decisive and somehow one shot them while the non combat lore supernal is under the dawns protective cares of your parry fills up the dawns essence pool so you come out mote positive</div> </div> </div> </div>You explicitly can't gain initiative by withering things that aren't actually your enemy. If you do something super meta-gamey like summon a weak demon and then &quot;betray&quot; it to farm initiative on it, then the ST gets to DM-slap you across the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:19:26-07:00","id":1396425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396347#post1396347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then toss a pebble as a decisive and somehow one shot them</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no part of the game that actively describes a pebble as a viable weapon, and a presumption that it could be just because there is not a specific exclusion is not engagement with the system in good faith.<br /> <br /> At least in cases where it is done for the sake of criticising a made up concern, rather than being employed as a stunt, and even that has some limits (if only because there's a point at which a projectile is unimpressive enough that the stunt can't really qualify as being sufficiently cool). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:03:13-07:00","id":1396431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396425#post1396425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no part of the game that actively describes a pebble as a viable weapon, and a presumption that it could be just because there is not a specific exclusion is not engagement with the system in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I could be totally sold on stunt where a PC ends a climatic duel by driving his pinky finger or a chopstick through the eye of his screaming nemesis before strolling away into the sunset (presumably putting on sunglasses while doing so). I personally would consider this a big old plus in favour of the system though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:09:23-07:00","id":1396433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396425#post1396425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no part of the game that actively describes a pebble as a viable weapon, and a presumption that it could be just because there is not a specific exclusion is not engagement with the system in good faith.<br /> <br /> At least in cases where it is done for the sake of criticising a made up concern, rather than being employed as a stunt, and even that has some limits (if only because there's a point at which a projectile is unimpressive enough that the stunt can't really qualify as being sufficiently cool).</div> </div> </div> </div>ok so when I have my 40 initiative dice and the target moves out of melee combat range I cant just chuck a rock as a decisive attack and roll those 40 initiative dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:45:03-07:00","id":1396435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396433#post1396433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok so when I have my 40 initiative dice and the target moves out of melee combat range I cant just chuck a rock as a decisive attack and roll those 40 initiative dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being beaned in the head with a decent sized rock can absolutely kill a person.<br /> <br /> Being beaned in the head with a <i>baseball</i> can kill a person.<br /> <br /> However, if you've got an almost certainly lethal amount of Initiative and try to apply it by tossing a feather at somebody, Orichalcum Rule applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:03:30-07:00","id":1396438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396433#post1396433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok so when I have my 40 initiative dice and the target moves out of melee combat range I cant just chuck a rock as a decisive attack and roll those 40 initiative dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're getting at, but ultimately this is a case of a player actively trying to break things. If you're stunting your decisive so that in-universe your attack couldn't possibly have killed the target, then you're just being disruptive at the table.<br /> <br /> It's a recurring pattern across all of the 3e Core that there is a ton of player freedom, but that the freedom comes with the responsibility to engage the game in good faith. Ex3 doesn't hold you by the hand, for better or worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:14:26-07:00","id":1396442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396438#post1396438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you're getting at, but ultimately this is a case of a player actively trying to break things. If you're stunting your decisive so that in-universe your attack couldn't possibly have killed the target, then you're just being disruptive at the table.<br /> <br /> It's a recurring pattern across all of the 3e Core that there is a ton of player freedom, but that the freedom comes with the responsibility to engage the game in good faith. Ex3 doesn't hold you by the hand, for better or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. In the particular case that this thread was based on I think it goes too far, where you have the freedom to make your character nearly invincible for next to no investment but theoretically the responsibility not to do that if it's not a major part of your character concept. Other stuff though like merit retainer spam or intentionally stunting your decisive kill shot as throwing a rock at their pinky toe are things you can reasonably expect a player not to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:49:24-07:00","id":1396702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396433#post1396433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok so when I have my 40 initiative dice and the target moves out of melee combat range I cant just chuck a rock as a decisive attack and roll those 40 initiative dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can take a Draw/Ready action to pick up a rock as a weapon with the &quot;Thrown (short)&quot; tag. I'd be tempted to throw on the &quot;Improvised&quot; tag, with the caveat that using Brawl or Melee is only applicable at Close range. If there's a rock available: otherwise it's a scavenge ammunition roll, then Draw/Ready. Then you make your Dexterity + Thrown attack roll (no Accuracy bonus on Decisive attacks). Then you roll your 39 dice of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-16-2020, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T01:58:06-07:00","id":1396834,"title":"","content":"This thread is very interesting to me because it covers the topic of the only area in which I feel Ex3 is genuinely poor as a game, and that's how it's incredibly hard to run a combat that walks the fine line between interesting and fair. And it's a real shame because the lack of good, interesting and useful adversaries basically kills the game for me these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T02:21:09-07:00","id":1396836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396347#post1396347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted 3e combat is, weird and abstract</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't. It's cinematic.<br /> <br /> It's not trying to recreate real life. It's helping you imagine something like a Wuxia movie scene. This relies on some abstractions, true. But I wouldn't call it &quot;weird&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396347#post1396347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can basically bring a defense 1 1 health level creature</div> </div> </div> </div>No such creature exists in canon. If your complaint is that you homebrewed something that doesn't work, then the problem is your homebrew. <br /> <br /> A cat has five health levels and Defense 3. Let's use that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396347#post1396347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and with a melee artifact weapon</div> </div> </div> </div>Melee Artifact weapons are the storied mystic creations of legend.<br /> <br /> Mjlonir. The Sword of Protection. Excalibur. The Master Sword.<br /> <br /> If your complaint is that having the Trident of Neptune or the Lasso of Truth makes it too easy to defeat house cats in combat... I don't know how to respond to that. Yes? I guess? Yes it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> withering attack it to get all the initiative you need </div> </div> </div>You <b>explicitly</b> can't do this as per the rules of the game. See &quot;FRIENDLY FIRE AND OTHER SHENANIGANS&quot; on page 194, the forth bullet point on &quot;Initiative Crash&quot; on page 193, and &quot;NONCOMBATANTS AND TRIVIAL OPPONENTS&quot; on page 208.<br /> <br /> You absolutely cannot do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> have the non combat person in your party decisive it to kill it off so your enemy doesnt do the same </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's legit.<br /> <br /> If there's a weak enemy on the field, the system sorta encourages you (outside of Trivial opponents) to deal with them using your weaker party members. This frees up your stronger party members to fight stronger enemies.<br /> <br /> In a genuine three way battle... well it's like when Shaft tried to arrest Sheev: the first thing Sheev did was kill the three weaker cops. It's a little &quot;meta&quot; to kill off weak foes so your other foes can't farm Initiative... but it's dramatic and cinematic.<br /> <br /> Killing your own allies to stop the enemy farming Initative is a little... extreme. Probably deserves its own thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then toss a pebble as a decisive and somehow one shot them </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with a Bullseye-esque Solar <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=RmqqNrg2cKg\" target=\"_blank\">tea-cupping</a> their foes.<br /> <br /> But see my post above about the potential problems with that tactic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while the non combat lore supernal is under the dawns protective cares of your parry fills up the dawns essence pool so you come out mote positive </div> </div> </div>Whilst mote farming is addressed by the rules above, it <i>is</i> pretty easy for a Dawn to War Lion Stance and a Twilight to Essence-Lending Method as the Dawn is bolstered with additional motes from Foe Cleaving Focus (although this is basically never mote positive) and Essence Gathering Temper (which is 1/scene unless you spec for it).<br /> <br /> This does lead to the Dawn coming out mote positive in all but the most serious fights.<br /> <br /> But let's look at that.<br /> <br /> 1. If two Solars work together<br /> 2. In fields they excel at as their Supernal area of focus<br /> 3. They will generally succeed in what they are attempting<br /> <br /> I... don't see the problem.<br /> <br /> (Not sure how the Twilight's Parry is filling the Dawn's Essence pool. Correct me if I've misunderstood.)<br /> <br /> I am not saying 3E is a perfect system. But if 2E taught us anything it's this:<br /> <br /> &quot;If doing X breaks the game, and stops you having fun, then don't do X.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:28:34-07:00","id":1397214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No such creature exists in canon. </div> </div> </div> </div>Virtuous Guardian of Flame 2 parry 2 health levels<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melee Artifact weapons are the storied mystic creations of legend.<br /> <br /> Mjlonir. The Sword of Protection. Excalibur. The Master Sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>they are which makes it funny when I beat them with a pebble and not my legendary weapon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <b>explicitly</b> can't do this as per the rules of the game. See &quot;FRIENDLY FIRE AND OTHER SHENANIGANS&quot; on page 194, the forth bullet point on &quot;Initiative Crash&quot; on page 193, and &quot;NONCOMBATANTS AND TRIVIAL OPPONENTS&quot; on page 208.<br /> <br /> You absolutely cannot do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>the fact that you actually have to make that a rule shows the inefficiencies of the system<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's a weak enemy on the field, the system sorta encourages you (outside of Trivial opponents) to deal with them using your weaker party members. This frees up your stronger party members to fight stronger enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whilst mote farming is addressed by the rules above, it <i>is</i> pretty easy for a Dawn to War Lion Stance and a Twilight to Essence-Lending Method as the Dawn is bolstered with additional motes from Foe Cleaving Focus (although this is basically never mote positive) and Essence Gathering Temper (which is 1/scene unless you spec for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence-Lending Method Will-Bolstering Method Essence Font Technique Immanent Solar Glory Flowing Essence Conversion Ancient Tongue Understanding Supernal Control Method with burning name dawn stands next to twilight while twilight uses burning name to superman eyebeam his foes while topping up the Dawns mote pool<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1396836#post1396836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If doing X breaks the game, and stops you having fun, then don't do X.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except if you dont all your players are now dead and the game is over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:05:25-07:00","id":1397219,"title":"","content":"You know tossing a pebble doesn't really work right? Initiative is fight momentum where your feints and lethal stabs and slashes create an opening to deal a finishing blow. So if I slash and stab(withering attacks) up to 40+ initiative there is a big opening, a high probability, I can end the fight with a thrust of my sword. If however, I fast draw a stuffed toy bear and smack my enemy in the face with it instead? That's a distract gambit, not me turning the toy into weapon projectile fired by a railgun that explodes his head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:08:47-07:00","id":1397220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397214#post1397214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence-Lending Method Will-Bolstering Method Essence Font Technique Immanent Solar Glory Flowing Essence Conversion Ancient Tongue Understanding Supernal Control Method with burning name dawn stands next to twilight while twilight uses burning name to superman eyebeam his foes while topping up the Dawns mote pool</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I'm getting this right, the combo is you activate Ancient Tongue Understanding, to get a free 1-2 successes on all your occult attacks with Burning Name. Then you maximize your dice pool with Supernal Control Method, which is normally once per scene but you reset it with Flowing Essence Conversion<br /> <br /> BUT you're also resetting Essence Lending Method's once per scene effect. So also once per turn you spend 5m, and roll Wits + Lore with recurring 10s, so about 6-7 motes, which you then transfer to your Dawn friend, along with at least one Willpower. Except if you want to bust your anima up to full iconic again to trigger Flowing Essence Conversion you're going to want to full excellency that roll, resulting in like 12-13 motes generated for 15m.<br /> <br /> So at the end of all this you're spending 25m per round and 6m at the start of combat, to generate about 13-14 motes between Immanent Solar Glory and Essence Lending, and make a full excellency attack with a mundane weapon, which can not be enhanced any further by any combat charms. It's not BAD exactly, if you're a loremaster/sorcerer who wants to fight by powering up the Dawn it works, but you'd be much better in combat by just being a Dawn yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397214#post1397214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except if you dont all your players are now dead and the game is over</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes <i>no </i>sense. In third edition if you don't make a crazy combo that 100% breaks the game, the game still runs perfectly fine. It's not like all the enemies in the book spam attacks that are &quot;perfect or die&quot; and the only way to survive is by breaking the game yourself.<br /> <br /> If you're just playing the game how it's supposed to be played it works perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:15:34-07:00","id":1397221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397220#post1397220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes <i>no </i>sense. In third edition if you don't make a crazy combo that 100% breaks the game, the game still runs perfectly fine. It's not like all the enemies in the book spam attacks that are &quot;perfect or die&quot; and the only way to survive is by breaking the game yourself.<br /> <br /> If you're just playing the game how it's supposed to be played it works perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like. Any game can be taken to absurdity by it's players, that's on the players. DnD 5e has a build allowing thousands of damage dealt in a single round by 20th level, it's unrealistic, absurd, and has no real impact on how the game plays or is enjoyed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:22:51-07:00","id":1397224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397221#post1397221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I like. Any game can be taken to absurdity by it's players, that's on the players. DnD 5e has a build allowing thousands of damage dealt in a single round by 20th level, it's unrealistic, absurd, and has no real impact on how the game plays or is enjoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can still have something that's bad for the game, like as I've said how it's just way too easy and tempting to make any character way too powerful in combat, but there needs to be a reasonable expectation that the players are going to cooperate. It's not like this is a competitive tabletop game where if there's a broken combo the whole tournament is ruined. You should at least have the expectation that somebody who takes Unusual Hide 5, Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, Stamina 5, and then heavy artifact plate to get a base soak of 27 before charms can be talked out of it if it's ruining the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:28:12-07:00","id":1397225,"title":"","content":"True, my upcoming game has one combat monster, the single point dawn. But he's vulnerable to multiple foes while the next biggest badass is an air aspected blind swordsman based off Zatoichi. The weakest is a twilight savant weaponsmith with a 3 in all physical stats and a 3 melee with a specialization in maces and 2 melee charms. I expect it to work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:44:48-07:00","id":1397228,"title":"","content":"The kind of crazy thing about Ex3 is that even that twilight is a pretty heavy hitter. He\u2019d totally wreck a storm god in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T21:52:49-07:00","id":1397230,"title":"","content":"Oh it's a little worse than that. She's using Five Edicts Dominion and Asphodel. Her story is very interesting but she's full of holes to exploit, especially socially. She's also not super interested in combat but wanted to survive heavier battles without being a burden. The reason for her artifact choices basically came down to the fact that soulsteel would be frowned on but she's such an obssessive character that she only cares about their craftsmanship and the rare material she'd never actually seen before. So she's optimised but only so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:06:10-07:00","id":1397232,"title":"","content":"Basically I don't expect her combat abilities to improve quickly at all. She's too focused on the lore, occult, and craft trees. Especially lore and craft, she really wants to know how everything works and to be able to craft new and amazing things. My night's a thief and the eclipse is a haughty duelist type. All in all though they are quite capable of crushing any singular opposition I might reasonably throw at them if they are able to gang up on it. Such is the prevailing theme of exalted. It's not a problem really, and it happens in most games. That badass dragon tends to be totally owned by that party of five adventures due to action economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T23:54:41-07:00","id":1397248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397214#post1397214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virtuous Guardian of Flame 2 parry 2 health levels</div> </div> </div> </div>So your response to my assertion that a Defence 1, 1 Health level creature doesn't exist... is to agree with me.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you are playing an Essence 1, <i>Intelligence</i> 1 Sorcerer, you can have a 2/2 creature. I agree with you too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they are which makes it funny when I beat them with a pebble and not my legendary weapon </div> </div> </div>I've addressed this reductio ad absurdum, as have others.<br /> <br /> But if you want a more productive answer, watch the <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X3gfFVmw0kA\" target=\"_blank\">Wizard's Duel</a>. It is absolutely legitimate to build Initiative with your deadly weapon, then end the fight with another weapon. <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=rgyitSlMtMY\" target=\"_blank\">Or vice versa</a>. Initiative represents your advantage in a fight, Decisive attacks are exploiting that advantage. <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=7sSBArpqAQI\" target=\"_blank\">Here's another combatant building Initiative with various attacks before he unleashes his finishing move with a completely different attack.</a> And <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=vdnA-ESWcPs\" target=\"_blank\">here is another, iconic, fight ending weapon change</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fact that you actually have to make that a rule shows the inefficiencies of the system </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in discussing this further. What do you mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except if you dont all your players are now dead and the game is over </div> </div> </div>What in Creation are you fighting?<br /> <br /> If you haven't played Tomb of Dreams, go back and play Tomb of Dreams with the pregen characters. That's Exalted. Starting Solars (with, like, 8 dice pools and no Artifacts) against gods, elementals and a Second Circle Demon.<br /> <br /> An ST literally can't accidentally kill a PC, because of the Withering/Decisive split.<br /> <br /> I just did <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">a mini session</a> of what Exalted looks like with no combat stats higher than 3, and only two Charms. You can fight pirates, navigate reefs, slay magical flying sharks, smash hurricanes, overcome powerful sea hags, slaughter the dreaded Chimera then sail away into the sunset. On Dex 3, Martial Arts 3, no Artifact and two Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-18-2020, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T02:47:10-07:00","id":1397254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397214#post1397214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the fact that you actually have to make that a rule shows the inefficiencies of the system<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is a game whose conceptions involved trying to represent the kind of stylistic, high concept action scenes you'd find in something like Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon.<br /> <br /> The Initiative system is an attempt to realise that conception by giving fights a focus on a shifting visual dynamic of who is winning with varied moment to moment tactical possibilities before suddenly bringing down a dangerous blow, rather than cutting things down to incentivize making every attack as lethal as possible.<br /> <br /> Trivial opponents and non-combatants is a contingency to maintain that focus, a reminder that the point is cinematic action in which those people don't belong.<br /> <br /> And yes, to preempt people that would not engage in their novel idea for representing that action in good faith and instead focus on finding technicalities to exploit. Even then, it's not actually that difficult to reconcile with the diegesis if one actually tries to picture the thing unfolding like an action scene, in which cutting down a helpless civilian is basically an afterthought and contributes nothing to the dynamic flow of the battle.<br /> <br /> What exactly do you want? Do you want the core book to have included the exact attack stats for a pebble and to have made them non-lethal so that you have a citation to assure you what is and is not a viable method of applying deadly force? That's not the combat system being weird, that's the writing team having the least bit of faith in their readers that they shall have an idea of what is and is not dangerous and apply their decisive attacks accordingly. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you're speaking as if there <i>are</i> stats for a pebble, and you find them unaccountably lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T05:48:14-07:00","id":1397276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397214#post1397214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence-Lending Method Will-Bolstering Method Essence Font Technique Immanent Solar Glory Flowing Essence Conversion Ancient Tongue Understanding Supernal Control Method with burning name dawn stands next to twilight while twilight uses burning name to superman eyebeam his foes while topping up the Dawns mote pool</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He's speaking the language of the gods.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:42:41-07:00","id":1397327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397276#post1397276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;He's speaking the language of the gods.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice meme bro<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T22:03:16-07:00","id":1397450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397219#post1397219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know tossing a pebble doesn't really work right? Initiative is fight momentum where your feints and lethal stabs and slashes create an opening to deal a finishing blow. So if I slash and stab(withering attacks) up to 40+ initiative there is a big opening, a high probability, I can end the fight with a thrust of my sword. If however, I fast draw a stuffed toy bear and smack my enemy in the face with it instead? That's a distract gambit, not me turning the toy into weapon projectile fired by a railgun that explodes his head.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok so I generated 40 initiative but I only have a melee option of doing damage and the target I want to decisive is now floating up in the air out of reach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T22:15:16-07:00","id":1397452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397220#post1397220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if I'm getting this right, the combo is you activate Ancient Tongue Understanding, to get a free 1-2 successes on all your occult attacks with Burning Name. Then you maximize your dice pool with Supernal Control Method, which is normally once per scene but you reset it with Flowing Essence Conversion<br /> <br /> BUT you're also resetting Essence Lending Method's once per scene effect. So also once per turn you spend 5m, and roll Wits + Lore with recurring 10s, so about 6-7 motes, which you then transfer to your Dawn friend, along with at least one Willpower. Except if you want to bust your anima up to full iconic again to trigger Flowing Essence Conversion you're going to want to full excellency that roll, resulting in like 12-13 motes generated for 15m.<br /> <br /> So at the end of all this you're spending 25m per round and 6m at the start of combat, to generate about 13-14 motes between Immanent Solar Glory and Essence Lending, and make a full excellency attack with a mundane weapon, which can not be enhanced any further by any combat charms. It's not BAD exactly, if you're a loremaster/sorcerer who wants to fight by powering up the Dawn it works, but you'd be much better in combat by just being a Dawn yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This makes <i>no </i>sense. In third edition if you don't make a crazy combo that 100% breaks the game, the game still runs perfectly fine. It's not like all the enemies in the book spam attacks that are &quot;perfect or die&quot; and the only way to survive is by breaking the game yourself.<br /> <br /> If you're just playing the game how it's supposed to be played it works perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya I dunno what I was thinking, giving a dawn access to unlimited motes of essence there by negating the limiting factor of how effective they are in combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T22:25:04-07:00","id":1397455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397452#post1397452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya I dunno what I was thinking, giving a dawn access to unlimited motes of essence there by negating the limiting factor of how effective they are in combat</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems not unlimited? You're spending 25 motes per round to give him like 13 motes per round. How many motes does your twilight have? 50? That's two rounds, of one combat, then you're done. Next scene you're mote tapped and useless. <br /> <br /> Even if that did work the way you think it does and you found a broken combo that gives unlimited motes, that's a broken combo. It's like finding an artifact that only mortals can attune to which combined with a mutation makes them invulnerable to damage and then saying &quot;Exalted are meaningless, the only things that matter in the world are mortals with this mutation and artifact.&quot; Like, clearly it's a mistake on the developers part to include that combo and should be house-ruled into not existing.<br /> <br /> Things like e Usurpation happened, if the mechanics don't reflect that<i> the mechanics are wrong, the setting is right.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 06-19-2020, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T00:12:01-07:00","id":1397463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397450#post1397450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok so I generated 40 initiative but I only have a melee option of doing damage and the target I want to decisive is now floating up in the air out of reach</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are SOL?<br /> <br /> You can't throw a pebble with Melee. Throwing a weapon is Thrown. If you have the Thrown ability, you probably have a knife or an axe or some weapon you can throw.<br /> <br /> Or you Stunt how you leap up to your foe. Use a Charm like Blazing Solar Bolt or Thunderbolt Attack Prana.<br /> <br /> If you have 40 Initiative, and your foe successfully Disengages one range band straight up into the air, you can't throw a pebble with Dexterity + Melee and Decisive them anyway. That's pretty much the point of Disengage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397452#post1397452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya I dunno what I was thinking, giving a dawn access to unlimited motes of essence there by negating the limiting factor of how effective they are in combat</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it fun?<br /> <br /> If it's fun, and works in your game, then carry on. As I said, two Supernal Solars both combining their expertise is meant to be world breakingly strong.<br /> <br /> But you seem to be complaining that <i>your</i> combo, which <i>you</i> came up with, isn't fun.<br /> <br /> No-one is forcing you to use that combo. No-one is suggesting you should use that combo. There is no reason for you to use that combo.<br /> <br /> If you don't like it, don't use it.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't meant to be played with mechanically optimised characters. It's meant to be played with interesting, story-driven characters. Which is why Volfer is Dex 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T00:19:04-07:00","id":1397465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397455#post1397455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things like e Usurpation happened, if the mechanics don't reflect that<i> the mechanics are wrong, the setting is right.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you ! I've not seen this stated enough, but I feel like games like Exalted particularly are very prone to this kind of problem, and I always find it odd when people try to re-explain the setting in retrospect instead of trying to fit the problematic mechanic in the setting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25272\" data-vbnamecard=\"25272\">Cypheriel</a> <br /> What's your point exactly ? I'd like to answer to you but basically you seem to be sort of provoking without expecting meaningful answers. How can we help you ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T00:27:38-07:00","id":1397468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397450#post1397450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok so I generated 40 initiative but I only have a melee option of doing damage and the target I want to decisive is now floating up in the air out of reach</div> </div> </div> </div>Well sure unless you have Iron Raptor Technique or Blazing Solar Bolt. If you don't, using Spitting Hand Technique to hurl a knife or that rock you were saving for your sling is a viable option. A casual toss of a pebble? Not so much. If you told me that's what you were doing when I was running a combat I'd laugh, especially if you were trying to toss a pebble at a guy range bands in the air. Initiative is a representaion of an opening for a strike, the more initiative the more sure the strike. A pebble could be swallowed I grant, but it might not be. The pebble that you are tossing, not firing from a slingshot, but tossing is not representative of a lethal attack. It is at best a distraction. But hey if you or your ST allow such absurdities that's both good for you and on you, not the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T03:20:47-07:00","id":1397486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1371898-exalted-vs-optimisation-split-from-exalted-arena?p=1397452#post1397452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya I dunno what I was thinking, giving a dawn access to unlimited motes of essence there by negating the limiting factor of how effective they are in combat</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think it's time to move on from this subject. This has reached the end of its conversational value.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}